

## Team of 7

The seven members split into two teams: a technical team of 4 who build the platform, and a business, compliance and governance team of 3 who own the plan, the business case and everything that keeps the project legal, safe and on track. Neither team needs the other's skills, but every sprint ends with a joint review.

**Technical team (4)**

| Member | Role | Owns | Backs up |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | Tech lead and backend developer | Architecture decisions, database, auth and roles, catalog API, enrollment, Stripe test-mode checkout | Member 2 |
| 2 | Backend developer | Video upload and playback, progress tracking, quizzes, certificates | Member 1 |
| 3 | Frontend developer (learner app) | Catalog, course page, player, quizzes, My learning dashboard | Member 4 |
| 4 | Full-stack developer and DevOps | Instructor course builder, admin screens, repo and CI/CD, hosting, automated tests | Member 3 |

**Business, compliance and governance team (3, no coding)**

| Member | Role | Owns | Backs up |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 5 | Project manager and governance lead | Scope and user stories, sprint board, meetings and minutes, RACI chart, risk register, decision log, final report and presentation | Member 7 |
| 6 | Business analyst and UX designer | Market and competitor research, business model and pricing, personas, Figma wireframes and prototypes, usability testing, go-to-market plan | Member 5 |
| 7 | Compliance and risk officer | Privacy law requirements, privacy policy and terms, copyright and instructor content licences, accessibility (WCAG) audit, data protection impact assessment, security and data-retention policies | Member 6 |

The business team also runs user acceptance testing: they write test scenarios from the user stories and test each release by hand, which frees the developers to build.



| Layer | Suggested choice | Replaces at scale |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Frontend | React or Next.js, responsive web or PWA (no native apps) | Separate web, iOS and Android apps |
| Backend | Node.js (Express or NestJS) or Django, REST API | Ten separate services behind a gateway |
| Database | PostgreSQL (one database, including a progress table) | Postgres plus Cassandra, Redis, OpenSearch |
| Video | Mux or Cloudinary free tier (handles transcoding and HLS) | Own transcoding pipeline, multi-CDN, DRM |
| Payments | Stripe in test mode | Stripe live with ledger and payouts |
| Search | Postgres full-text search | OpenSearch |
| Hosting | Vercel (frontend) and Render or Railway (backend, database) | Kubernetes in two regions |
| CI/CD | GitHub Actions | Same |

Kafka, live classes, DRM, coding sandboxes and recommendations stay in the design document as future work rather than being built.

